<title>USA: TABLE-First Essex Bancorp Q2 net increase.</title>
<headline>TABLE-First Essex Bancorp Q2 net increase.</headline>
<dateline>ANDOVER, Mass. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the Three Months  For the Six Months</p>
<p>				  Ended June 30,    Ended June 30,</p>
<p>			     1997	 1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p>Interest Income:</p>
<p> Net Interest Income   9,595	6,477     18,752     12,588</p>
<p>Provision for Possible Loan Losses</p>
<p>				 510	  326	1,020	  815</p>
<p>Non-Interest Income:</p>
<p>Gain on Sales of Mortgage Loans</p>
<p>				 556	  453	  918	  930</p>
<p>Gain</p>
<p> (Loss) on Sale of Investments(3)   ---	   49	  ---</p>
<p> Net Income		2,526	2,130	4,673	3,884</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share	.33	  .35	  .61	  .63</p>
<p>Average Common and Equivalent</p>
<p>Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>			 7,769,658  6,154,310  7,737,953  6,158,390</p>
<p>(Dollars in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  First Essex Bancorp Inc said most of the increase in net income reflects reflects the acquisition of Finest Financial Corp in December 1996.</p>
